# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: entmake-subclass-group-order -- the CADs reject ENTMAKE data whose groups do not follow their own subclass marker; clautolisp accepts it
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: entity-mutation-parity
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-27

* Measured (probe entity-defaults, 2026-10-27)

ENTMAKEX with every subclass marker FIRST, then all the groups:

| data                                                        | AutoCAD 2022 | BricsCAD V25 | clautolisp |
|-------------------------------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+------------|
| ARC: AcDbCircle AcDbArc, then 10 40 50 51                    | created      | rejected     | created    |
| ATTDEF: AcDbText AcDbAttributeDefinition, then 10 40 1 3 2 70 | rejected     | rejected     | created    |
| ATTRIB (after an INSERT 66 1): the same                       | rejected     | rejected     | created    |

The same groups each after its own marker are created everywhere (the
"ordered" cases). So a group is read as belonging to the subclass whose
marker precedes it, and one that subclass does not have fails the
ENTMAKE -- BricsCAD everywhere, AutoCAD at least for the attributes.

* To do

1. Probe more: which families / misplacements each product rejects
   (AutoCAD's ARC case says its rule is narrower than BricsCAD's).
2. Per-subclass group sets in the entity-family registry, and ENTMAKE
   rejecting (nil, as for a missing required group) per the dialect's
   product.

* Batched probe prepared 2026-10-29 (branch prep-pending-probes)

probes/sources/probe-pending-divergences.lsp (suite "pending-divergences",
group entmake-order) captures this on real hardware. Run it via
probe:suite:{autocad,bricscad}:windows / :macos when the Windows runner is next
online (one session covers all three data-blocked issues). clautolisp baseline
validated 2026-10-29.
